# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the code is
#   intended to run in multiple environments; otherwise, check them in:
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in case of collaboration, if lock is used, it may cause conflicts; so uncomment if needed.
# lock

# poetry
#   Poetry uses pyproject.toml to manage dependencies and has a poetry.lock file.
#   It is recommended to include poetry.lock in version control.
# poetry.lock

# pdm
#   PDM stores local configuration in .pdm.toml
.pdm.toml
.pdm-python
.pdm-build/

# Pipfile
#   Pipfile.lock is ignored if it's a library, but generally checked in.

